    fg_cell_count: 4-9 (fraction 0.25-0.56 of panel)
    connected_components: 1-2
  case_types:
    complement: right mask == bitwise NOT of left mask (they tile the full panel); ~55% of examples
    overlap: right mask shares >=1 cell with left mask; ~45% of examples
  output:
    size: 4x4 (one panel)
    complement_case: left_fg + right_fg fill every cell (two-color mosaic)
    overlap_case: output == left panel unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction, cases built separately
  steps:
    1. Pick panel H=4, W=4. Choose left_color=1, right_color from {2,3,6,7}, sep_color=5, bg=0.
    2. Flip a coin for complement vs overlap case.
    3. Complement case - randomly generate a binary mask M on the 4x4 panel with fg_count in [4,12]; left=M filled with left_color, right=NOT(M) filled with right_color.
    4. Overlap case - generate left mask L (fg_count 7-12); generate right mask R (fg_count 4-9) ensuring at least 1 cell overlaps L (i.e. L AND R != empty). Retry if no overlap.
    5. Assemble input as [left_panel | sep_column | right_panel] (9 cols wide).
